course: dictionary
lesson: 2763
title: Discomfort: the gentle word for pain
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Doctors and nurses often choose gentle words so that you are not frightened. When a nurse says, «You may feel some discomfort», she is telling you that it could hurt a little. Discomfort means a feeling of mild pain, or of not being comfortable in your body.
explain: Discomfort can also be a feeling inside you, not in your body. A child who is embarrassed or uneasy feels discomfort too. Use the context clues to decide which meaning fits: is someone hurt, or is someone worried and embarrassed?
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «You may feel some discomfort» becomes «You may feel some mild pain». Does it still make sense? If it does, you have the right meaning, and you know to get ready.
fact: Discomfort is a noun. You can have one discomfort, or several discomforts.
fact: «Discomfort» means a feeling of mild pain, or of not being comfortable in your body.
fact: «Discomfort» can also mean a feeling of worry or embarrassment.
fact: In a doctor's mouth, «some discomfort» is a calm way of saying «it may hurt».
fact: Doctors say «a procedure» for an operation, and «an adverse event» for a mistake that harms a patient.
exercise: When a nurse says «You may feel some discomfort», what does she mean? | *It may hurt a little | Please sit down quietly | You will feel very happy and relaxed | The room is too hot
exercise: Lily felt discomfort when everyone stared at her spilt drink. What feeling does discomfort show here? | Joy | Hunger | Sleepiness | *Embarrassment
exercise: Find and copy one word from «You may feel some discomfort» that means a feeling of mild pain. | *discomfort | feel | some | may
test: The doctor said, «This procedure may cause some discomfort.» What does procedure mean in this sentence? | A loud noise | *An operation | A type of bread | A cosy blanket
test: In a story, Sam felt discomfort as he sat red-faced at the front of the class. What does discomfort show about Sam? | Hunger | *Worry and embarrassment | Great strength | A wish to sing
exam: Mia's dentist says, «You may feel some discomfort», so what should Mia expect? | *A little pain | A free ice cream | A big party | Nothing at all, not even a tickle
